m converts experiences into a hybrid memory graph that flexibly links time-aware gists and facts. 2) Online inference, where REMem employs an agentic retriever with carefully curated tools for iterative retrieval over the memory graph. Comprehensive evaluation across four episodic memory benchmarks shows that REMem substantially outperforms state-of-the-art memory systems such as Mem0 and HippoRAG 2, showing 3.4% and 13.4% absolute improvements on episodic recollection and reasoning tasks, respectively. Moreover, REMem also demonstrates more robust refusal behavior for unanswerable questions.\n\nView arXiv page View PDF GitHub 30 auto Add to collection--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nICLR 2026 Graph Heavy Track and Key Takeaways | Artemiy Vereshinskiy posted on the topic | LinkedIn (https://www.linkedin.com/posts/onepx_iclr2026-graphml-gnn-activity-7457338514784047104-K_U8)\nciteturn31904search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; BrowseNet: Graph-Based Associative Memory for Contextual Information Retrieval https://github.com/bisect-group/BrowseNet ... REMem: Reasoning with Episodic Memory in Language Agents https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.13530\nNeural Graduated Assignment for Maximum Common Edge Subgraphs https://openreview.net/forum?id=ZVlTIyRe35 8. Modality-free Graph In-context Alignment https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.13434 9. BrowseNet: Graph-Based Associative Memory for Contextual Information Retrieval https://github.com/bisect-group/BrowseNet\n\nLike\n\nArtemiy Vereshinskiy 3mo\n\n16. Flash-Searcher: Fast and Effective WebAgents via DAG-Based Parallel Execution https://github.com/OPPO-PersonalAI/Flash-Searcher 17. MomaGraph: State-Aware Unified Scene Graphs with Vision-Language Models for Embodied Task Planning https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.16909 18. CoMEM: Compositional Concept-Graph Memory for Vision-Language Adaptation https://openreview.net/forum?id=xp7wDU9JBW\n\nLike\n\nArtemiy Vereshinskiy 3mo\n\n10. LINEARRAG: 